{"authored" [{"question" "q-124871" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}2y\\,dx+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,dy+3z\\,dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the curve $r(t)=\\,i+t\\,j+{t}^{2}\\,k$ for $t\\in [1,3]?$" "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-124871/review.json" "file_sha256" "71e372b8900659d39d9e18c3fedda5492bc8b8e62c82a5c3b8f9a58f6d758e07" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-124871/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "93f77f44ca76f547a096a35ecb7aad38c805c7cf49fe3cdc40753d429e66bced" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-124871/verification.json" "basis" 1883 "rationale" "The original source correctly substitutes 3t^2*(2t), then incorrectly simplifies it to6t^2. Correct pullback is6t^3 and integral120. Preserve the original prompt and four current distractor answer identities, replace the defective study alternative with the already stored correct exponent, new field identity with existing mathematically correct answer identity retained, preserve raw source and actual Correct probe grade as evidence."} {"question" "q-124871" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Along $C$, $x(t)=1$, $y(t)=t$, and $z(t)=t^2$, so $x'(t)=0$, $y'(t)=1$, and $z'(t)=2t$. Substitute both the coordinates and their derivatives:\n\n$$\\int_C 2y\\,dx+\\ln x\\,dy+3z\\,dz\n=\\int_1^3\\left(2t\\cdot0+\\ln(1)\\cdot1+3t^2\\cdot2t\\right)\\,dt\n=\\int_1^3 6t^3\\,dt.$$\n\nThus the equivalent integral is $\\int_1^3 6t^3\\,dt$, and its value is $[\\tfrac32t^4]_1^3=120$.\n\nThe original source accepted $\\int_1^3 6t^2\\,dt$ and its worked solution changed $3t^2\\cdot2t$ into $6t^2$. That simplification loses a factor of $t$. The study choice replaces that exponent with $3$; all other original choices are retained." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-124871/review.json" "file_sha256" "71e372b8900659d39d9e18c3fedda5492bc8b8e62c82a5c3b8f9a58f6d758e07" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-124871/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "93f77f44ca76f547a096a35ecb7aad38c805c7cf49fe3cdc40753d429e66bced" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-124871/verification.json" "basis" 1883 "rationale" "The original source correctly substitutes 3t^2*(2t), then incorrectly simplifies it to6t^2. Correct pullback is6t^3 and integral120. Preserve the original prompt and four current distractor answer identities, replace the defective study alternative with the already stored correct exponent, new field identity with existing mathematically correct answer identity retained, preserve raw source and actual Correct probe grade as evidence."} {"question" "q-124871" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{3}6t^{3}\\,dt"] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-124871/review.json" "file_sha256" "71e372b8900659d39d9e18c3fedda5492bc8b8e62c82a5c3b8f9a58f6d758e07" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-124871/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "93f77f44ca76f547a096a35ecb7aad38c805c7cf49fe3cdc40753d429e66bced" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-124871/verification.json" "basis" 1883 "rationale" "The original source correctly substitutes 3t^2*(2t), then incorrectly simplifies it to6t^2. Correct pullback is6t^3 and integral120. Preserve the original prompt and four current distractor answer identities, replace the defective study alternative with the already stored correct exponent, new field identity with existing mathematically correct answer identity retained, preserve raw source and actual Correct probe grade as evidence."}] "sources" [{"question" "q-124885" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}x{y}^{2}\\,dx+\\frac{1}{x}\\,dy,$ where $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+t\\,j$ for $t\\in [1,3]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124885" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\frac{1}{t},\\,y(t)=t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,j \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}x{y}^{2}\\,dx+\\frac{1}{x}\\,dy & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}x{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+\\frac{1}{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(x{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{1}{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{t}\\cdot {t}^{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}})+\\frac{1}{(\\frac{1}{t})}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}-\\frac{1}{t}+t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{t}^{2}-1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124885" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "84f39962c9d9119c2e3886c938bb13e6a49031d686f09cd2ff8017e3fb391a17"} {"question" "q-124885" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124885" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{3}2t\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{t-1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{t}^{2}+1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{t}^{2}-1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124885" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{t}^{2}-1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124875" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}(x+y)\\,dx+(x+2)\\,dy,$ where $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=(t-2)\\,i+({t}^{3}-t)\\,j$ for $t\\in [1,2]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124875" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=t-2,\\,y(t)={t}^{3}-t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-2)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-t)\\,j \\\\  & =i+(3{t}^{2}-1)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(x+y)\\,dx+(x+2)\\,dy & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(x+y)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+(x+2)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}((x+y)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+(x+2)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(t-2+{t}^{3}-t)\\cdot 1+(t-2+2)\\cdot (3{t}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{t}^{3}-2+3{t}^{3}-t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}4{t}^{3}-t-2\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124875" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "84f39962c9d9119c2e3886c938bb13e6a49031d686f09cd2ff8017e3fb391a17"} {"question" "q-124875" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124875" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{2}4{t}^{3}+t-2\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{2}4{t}^{3}-2\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{2}4{t}^{3}-3t-2\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{2}4{t}^{3}-t-2\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{2}t(4{t}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124875" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{1}^{2}4{t}^{3}-t-2\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124872" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}(x-2y)\\,dx+x\\,dy,$ where $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=(t+1)\\,i-2{t}^{2}\\,j$ for $t\\in [-1,1]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124872" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=t+1,\\,y(t)=-2{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2{t}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =i+(-4t)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(x-2y)\\,dx+x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x-2y)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}((x-2y)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(t+1-2\\cdot (-2{t}^{2}))\\cdot 1+(t+1)\\cdot (-4t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}t+1+4{t}^{2}-4{t}^{2}-4t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}1-3t\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124872" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "84f39962c9d9119c2e3886c938bb13e6a49031d686f09cd2ff8017e3fb391a17"} {"question" "q-124872" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124872" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}1-3t-8{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}1-3t\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}1-4t\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}1-5t\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}8{t}^{2}+4t+1\\,\\text{d}t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124872" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}1-3t\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124878" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}(x-y)\\,dx+(y-x)\\,dy,$ where $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124878" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y(t)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(x-y)\\,dx+(y-x)\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(x-y)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+(y-x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}((x-y)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+(y-x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t))\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-4{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}4({cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124878" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "84f39962c9d9119c2e3886c938bb13e6a49031d686f09cd2ff8017e3fb391a17"} {"question" "q-124878" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124878" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124878" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124882" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}xy\\,dx+x\\,dy,$ where $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)={e}^{t}\\,i+{e}^{t+1}\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,1]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124882" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{t},\\,y(t)={e}^{t+1}.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t+1})\\,j \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\,i+{e}^{t+1}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}xy\\,dx+x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}xy\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(xy\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{t+1}\\cdot {e}^{t}+{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{3t+1}+{e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124882" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "84f39962c9d9119c2e3886c938bb13e6a49031d686f09cd2ff8017e3fb391a17"} {"question" "q-124882" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124882" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{3t+1}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{3t+1}+{e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{3t}+{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{5t+2}\\,\\text{d}t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124882" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{3t+1}+{e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124871" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}2y\\,dx+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,dy+3z\\,dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the curve $r(t)=\\,i+t\\,j+{t}^{2}\\,k$ for $t\\in [1,3]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124871" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=1,\\,y(t)=t,\\,z(t)={t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =\\,j+2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}2y\\,dx+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,dy+3z\\,dz & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}2y\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+3z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(2y\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+3z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}2t\\cdot (0)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡1\\cdot (1)+3{t}^{2}\\cdot (2t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}6{t}^{2}\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124871" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "84f39962c9d9119c2e3886c938bb13e6a49031d686f09cd2ff8017e3fb391a17"} {"question" "q-124871" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124871" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{3}3{t}^{2}+2\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{3}5\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+2\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{3}6{t}^{2}\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{3}{t}^{2}+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{3}{t}^{3}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,dt"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124871" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{1}^{3}6{t}^{2}\\,dt"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}{x}^{3}\\,dx+z\\,dy+y\\,dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the helix $r(t)=t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,\\pi ]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=t,\\,y(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,z(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}{x}^{3}\\,dx+z\\,dy+y\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{x}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+z\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+y\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({x}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+z\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+y\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{t}^{3}\\cdot (1)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{t}^{3}+{cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{t}^{3}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "84f39962c9d9119c2e3886c938bb13e6a49031d686f09cd2ff8017e3fb391a17"} {"question" "q-124809" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124809" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡t+1\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{3}⁡t\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{t}^{2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{t}^{3}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,dt"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124809" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{t}^{3}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,dt"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124832" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}-y\\,dx+x\\,dy+z\\,dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the helix $r(t)=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+t\\,k$ for $t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{3}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124832" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y(t)=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,z(t)=t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,k \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}-y\\,dx+x\\,dy+z\\,dz & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}-y\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}(-y\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)+t\\cdot 1\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}t+2{sin}^{2}⁡t+2{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}t+2\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124832" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "84f39962c9d9119c2e3886c938bb13e6a49031d686f09cd2ff8017e3fb391a17"} {"question" "q-124832" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124832" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}t+2\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}{t}^{2}+9\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}{t}^{2}+{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}{t}^{2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,dt"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124832" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}t+2\\,dt"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124823" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}z\\,dx+y\\,dy-x\\,dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the curve $r(t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124823" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y(t)={t}^{2},\\,z(t)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2t\\,j+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}z\\,dx+y\\,dy-x\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}z\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt-x\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(z\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}-x\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+{t}^{2}\\cdot (2t)-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2{t}^{3}-9{sin}^{2}⁡t-9{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2{t}^{3}-9\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124823" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "84f39962c9d9119c2e3886c938bb13e6a49031d686f09cd2ff8017e3fb391a17"} {"question" "q-124823" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124823" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2{t}^{2}+3{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2{t}^{2}+3{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2{t}^{3}-9\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t-{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{t}^{4}-2\\,dt"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124823" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2{t}^{3}-9\\,dt"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124865" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}{y}^{2}\\,dx+x\\,dy+z\\,dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the line $r(t)=t\\,i+2t\\,j+3t\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,5]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124865" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=t,\\,y(t)=2t,\\,z(t)=3t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t)\\,k \\\\  & =\\,i+2\\,j+3\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}{y}^{2}\\,dx+x\\,dy+z\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}({y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}4{t}^{2}\\cdot (1)+t\\cdot (2)+3t\\cdot (3)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}4{t}^{2}+11t\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124865" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "84f39962c9d9119c2e3886c938bb13e6a49031d686f09cd2ff8017e3fb391a17"} {"question" "q-124865" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124865" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{5}2{t}^{4}-5t\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{5}4t+5\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{5}4{t}^{2}+11t\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{5}{t}^{2}+10t+5\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{5}{t}^{3}+2\\,dt"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124865" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{5}4{t}^{2}+11t\\,dt"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-81177" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}y\\,dx+x\\,dy,$ where $C$ is a portion of the ellipse parametrized by $r(t)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{12},\\frac{\\pi }{4}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-81177" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y(t)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\n.\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can calculate the line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}y\\,dx+x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /4}y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /4}(y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /4}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /4}{cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t){|}_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =4-2 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-81177" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "84f39962c9d9119c2e3886c938bb13e6a49031d686f09cd2ff8017e3fb391a17"} {"question" "q-81177" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-81177" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-81177" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-81097" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}-y\\,dx+x\\,dy,$ where $C$ is a portion of the circle parametrized by $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,\\pi ].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-81097" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can calculate the line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}-y\\,dx+x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }-y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(-y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\,dt \\\\  & =t{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\pi -0 \\\\  & =\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-81097" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "84f39962c9d9119c2e3886c938bb13e6a49031d686f09cd2ff8017e3fb391a17"} {"question" "q-81097" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-81097" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-81097" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pi "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-90844" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}-\\frac{1}{z}\\,dx+x\\,dy+dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the helix parametrized by $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+t\\,j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,\\pi ].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-90844" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y(t)=t,\\,z(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can calculate the line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}-\\frac{1}{z}\\,dx+x\\,dy+dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }-\\frac{1}{z}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{z}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot 1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\pi +2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -0 \\\\  & =\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-90844" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "84f39962c9d9119c2e3886c938bb13e6a49031d686f09cd2ff8017e3fb391a17"} {"question" "q-90844" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-90844" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2+\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "2-\\pi "] ["math" "2\\pi "] ["math" "\\pi "] ["math" "\\pi +2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-90844" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pi "] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124721" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}y\\,dx+x\\,dy+z\\,dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the curve $r(t)=t\\,i+(t-1)\\,j+{e}^{t}\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,1].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124721" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=t,\\,y(t)=t-1,\\,z(t)={e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-1)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,k \\\\  & =i+j+{e}^{t}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}y\\,dx+x\\,dy+z\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(y\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(t-1)\\cdot (1)+t\\cdot (1)+{e}^{t}\\cdot ({e}^{t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{2t}+2t-1\\,dt \\\\  & =(\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{2}+{t}^{2}-t){|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}+1-1)-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124721" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "84f39962c9d9119c2e3886c938bb13e6a49031d686f09cd2ff8017e3fb391a17"} {"question" "q-124721" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124721" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{5{e}^{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}+1"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-124721" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-81171" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}\\frac{(2x+y+1)}{x}\\,dx+dy,$ where $C$ is a portion of the parabola parametrized by $r(t)=t\\,i+({t}^{2}-1)\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-81171" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=t,\\,y(t)={t}^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-1)\\,j \\\\  & =i+2t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can calculate the line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\frac{2x+y+1}{x}\\,dx+dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{2x+y+1}{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{2x+y+1}{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{2t+{t}^{2}-1+1}{t}+2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2+t+2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2+3t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[2t+\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =[2(2)+\\frac{3}{2}(2)^{2}]-[0] \\\\  & =[4+6] \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-81171" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "84f39962c9d9119c2e3886c938bb13e6a49031d686f09cd2ff8017e3fb391a17"} {"question" "q-81171" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-81171" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "q-81171" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9d33368e373bbd8bea981a431783adb52575a8eb8bfbd8b21c9a01cb6e56727"} {"question" "e-7118" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Construct a definite integral that is equivalent to $\\displaystyle \\int\\limits_C (x^2+y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x + x\\,\\mathrm{d}y,$ where $C$ is parametrized by $\\mathbf{r}(t) = t\\,\\mathbf{i} + t^2\\,\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in\\left[0,1\\right].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/example-7118.json" "file_sha256" "aa696d5681c10cd6e917c34f3c304a165e29adbbc6e1e28ef4351d09d4aaecea"} {"question" "e-7118" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t) = t, \\qquad\ny(t) = t^2.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $\\mathbf r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =i+2t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}({x}^{2}+y)\\,dx+x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+y)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(({x}^{2}+y)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({t}^{2}+{t}^{2})\\cdot 1+t\\cdot 2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{t}^{2}+2{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/example-7118.json" "file_sha256" "aa696d5681c10cd6e917c34f3c304a165e29adbbc6e1e28ef4351d09d4aaecea"} {"question" "e-9517" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Construct a definite integral that is equivalent to $\\displaystyle \\int\\limits_C x^3\\,\\mathrm{d}x + z\\,\\mathrm{d}y + y\\,\\mathrm{d}z,$ where $C$ is a portion of the helix $\\mathbf{r}(t)=2t\\,\\mathbf{i} + \\cos t\\,\\mathbf{j} + \\sin t\\,\\mathbf{k}$ for $t\\in[0,\\pi]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/example-9517.json" "file_sha256" "4893bed5e5c553818eba4509c41c7dff747174930db6e99092a8c91f43f422df"} {"question" "e-9517" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t) =2t, \\qquad \ny(t) = \\cos t , \\qquad \nz(t) = \\sin t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $\\mathbf r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}{x}^{3}\\,dx+z\\,dy+y\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{x}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+z\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+y\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({x}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+z\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+y\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2t)^{3}\\cdot (2)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }16{t}^{3}-{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }16{t}^{3}+({cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }16{t}^{3}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/example-9517.json" "file_sha256" "4893bed5e5c553818eba4509c41c7dff747174930db6e99092a8c91f43f422df"} {"question" "e-9528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int\\limits_C y\\,\\mathrm{d}x -x\\,\\mathrm{d}y ,$ where $C$ is a portion of the ellipse parametrized by $\\mathbf{r}(t)=\\cos t\\,\\mathbf{i} + 3\\sin t\\,\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in[0,\\pi].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/example-9528.json" "file_sha256" "498d1b4acf0f910d0901a473386e16fd7b021a1b3df32c939a49f80e427c380f"} {"question" "e-9528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t) = \\cos t, \\qquad\ny(t) = 3\\sin t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $\\mathbf r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}y\\,dx-x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt-x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\cdot 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }-3{sin}^{2}⁡t-3{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & =-3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & =-3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\,dt \\\\  & =-3{t|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-3\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/example-9528.json" "file_sha256" "498d1b4acf0f910d0901a473386e16fd7b021a1b3df32c939a49f80e427c380f"} {"question" "q-124871" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{1}^{3}6{t}^{2}\\,dt"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058775/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "a9670442b855cdce930d47a86ca9d5f454cff14239376ea2e344c7e9096842d0" "reviewer_session" "/root/recover_multivariable_saved_integral/source-feedback-review" "rationale" "Observed real Correct grade accepts displayed b, whose value is integral6t². The source worked solution also prints6t² after3t²*(2t). This identifies the authentic accepted source key only: it is mathematically false for the raw prompt, whose true answer is integral6t³=120. Preserve original mathematical solver answer, create source-backed import, then apply verified versioned study correction." "bindings" {"problem" "604277ff06e37ff4cb5a3e74ff92e718fcee953fa80b1b0fdaa03326b3df0c62" "worked_solution" "48e0b63f7300779018ac69865cebf2028f66b316ed76212a45b8846b039014d5" "original_field" "35bbe62f4477c6197d67af948ceec7740